WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
So router agents are things where you have an agent that essentially uses a router

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.200
that sits in front of it and calls other functions or potentially other agents.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.440
It can be workflows. It can be agents. It can be whatever.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.160
And the router that sits in front of it doesn't have to be an agent.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.460
It can be an if-then statement, an algorithm, whatever.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:22.280
And then you evolve from router agents into these things called orchestration agents.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:28.000
So orchestration agents are, essentially, like—you can think about the router. Router agents...

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.640
...go one way. With orchestration agents, you come into the router,

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.200
or in this case the orchestrator, and it can get information back from the agents.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.040
They can kind of work like this.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:41.840
So it goes back and forth between the different things and accomplishes more complex tasks.
